
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Ex 03: Responsive Webpage Layout</title>

<style>
* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

body {
    font-family: Georgia, Garamond, serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background-color: #f4f6f9;
    color: #333333;
}

header {
    background-color: #1e222b;
    padding: 30px 20px;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

.container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    width: 90%;
    margin: 40px auto;
}

main {
    display: block;
}

.hero-banner {
    width: 100%;
    height: 300px;
    background-color: lightblue;
    background-image: url("https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498050108023-c5249f4df085");
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 35px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

.main-title {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: bolder;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    text-shadow: 3px 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

.hero-banner h2 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    padding: 15px 25px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px #000000;
    text-align: center;
}

.section-heading {
    color: #2c3e50;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #ff9f0a;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
}

.magazine-layout {
    column-count: 3;
    column-gap: 30px;
    column-rule: 1px dashed #cccccc;
    text-align: justify;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
}

.magazine-layout p {
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    font-size: 17px;
}

.highlight-text {
    display: inline;
    background-color: #fff3cd;
    font-weight: bold;
    padding: 0 4px;
}

.nav-menu {
    margin-top: 15px;
    list-style-type: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 15px;
}

.nav-menu a {
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: bold;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

.nav-menu a:link {
    color: #ffffff;
    background-color: #34495e;
}

.nav-menu a:visited {
    color: #e2e8f0;
    background-color: #4a5568;
}

.nav-menu a:hover {
    color: #111111;
    background-color: #ff9f0a;
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.nav-menu a:active {
    color: #ffffff;
    background-color: #f44336;
}

.features-box {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    padding: 25px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
    margin-top: 30px;
}

.custom-list {
    list-style-type: circle;
    padding-left: 30px;
    margin-top: 15px;
}

.custom-list li {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 18px;
}

footer {
    background-color: #1e222b;
    color: #ffffff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 50px;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
    .magazine-layout {
        column-count: 2;
    }

    .main-title {
        font-size: 28px;
    }
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
    .magazine-layout {
        column-count: 1;
    }

    .nav-menu {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: stretch;
    }

    .hero-banner {
        height: 200px;
    }

    .hero-banner h2 {
        font-size: 20px;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
    <h1 class="main-title">Modern Design Insights</h1>

    <nav>
        <ul class="nav-menu">
            <li><a href="#home">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#articles">Articles</a></li>
            <li><a href="#layouts">Layout Specs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact Us</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
</header>

<div class="container">

    <div class="hero-banner" id="home">
        <h2>Exploring HTML5 & CSS3 Properties</h2>
    </div>

    <main id="articles">

        <h3 class="section-heading">
            Featured Editorial (Multi-Column Layout)
        </h3>

        <div class="magazine-layout">

            <p>
                Cascading Style Sheets (CSS3) has revolutionized how
                layout design operates on modern screens.
                By utilizing advanced structural parameters like the
                multicolumn layout grid mechanism, webpage
                architects can easily wrap long-form data across
                sequential vertical paths seamlessly.
                This mimics high-end print publishing styles without
                breaking data accessibility rules.
            </p>

            <p>
                Managing element spatial dynamics is critical. Margins
                define empty whitespace structural areas outside
                borders, while paddings preserve internal breathing
                boundaries inside components.
                <span class="highlight-text">Understanding the box model</span>
                ensures fluid elements scale proportionally across devices,
                guaranteeing that elements remain well-organized regardless
                of viewing scale.
            </p>

            <p>
                Typography holds equal priority alongside positional
                layouts. CSS3 properties like letter-spacing,
                font-weight modifiers, font-style variants, and
                ambient text-shadow fields elevate unpolished copy
                into visually striking digital designs.
                Using web-safe fallbacks keeps layouts robust across platforms.
            </p>

        </div>
    </main>

    <section class="features-box" id="layouts">

        <h4 class="section-heading">
            Core Layout Specifications Explored
        </h4>

        <p>
            During this assignment iteration, the structural elements
            are tested against standard presentation benchmarks:
        </p>

        <ul class="custom-list">

            <li>
                <strong>Normal Flow:</strong>
                The base operational standard tracking block elements
                sequentially downward.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>CSS3 Multicolumn Rules:</strong>
                Splitting clean text tracks automatically using
                structural column configurations.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>State Engine Links:</strong>
                Monitoring element responsiveness through customized
                unvisited, visited, hover, and active states.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Display Switches:</strong>
                Alternating formatting logic between inline text
                containers and structural block spaces gracefully.
            </li>

        </ul>
    </section>

</div>

<footer id="contact">
    <p>
        &copy; 2026 Department of Web Engineering.
        All Rights Reserved. Ex.No:03 - Portfolio.
    </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
